\value{
The path(s) to the generated output file(s) (invisibly).  A single
string when one format is requested; a character vector when multiple
formats are requested.
}
\description{
Creates a PDF, HTML, or LaTeX document summarising key parameters of the
object.  The layout and content are controlled by the \code{template}
argument.

For a \code{technology}, the datasheet describes that technology. For a
\code{repository}, \code{model}, or solved \code{scenario}, give the
technology via \code{name = }: the same datasheet is produced, but the
embedded levelized cost is computed for that container / solution (the
\code{scenario} method uses the \emph{ex-post} cost from the solved model).

\strong{Without} \code{name}, the container methods report the whole object:
\describe{
\item{\code{model} / \code{repository}}{a full model report -- the
configuration (regions, horizon, calendar, discount), an inventory of
commodities / supplies / demands / trade / constraints, the process
availability windows chart, and every technology and storage described
one-by-one (diagram + key parameters).}
\item{\code{scenario}}{a results overview of the solved scenario -- solve
status and objective, generation / capacity / new-capacity mixes (via
\code{\link{getMix}} and \code{autoplot}), a sub-annual dispatch profile
when the calendar has one, emissions and cost tables.}
}
}
\section{Functions}{
\itemize{
\item \code{report(commodity)}: Element datasheets. Every element class -- commodity,
supply, demand, trade, import, export, weather, tax, subsidy,
constraint, calendar, horizon, config, costs -- has a \code{report()}
method rendering a one-object datasheet from its shipped
\verb{report_<class>.Rmd} template. The default template is the class name;
an object-level default can be stored in \code{misc$report} (the techspec
\verb{report:} key), and an explicit \verb{template =} always wins. From a
container, \code{report(mod, name = "X")} finds the element of any class
(pass \verb{class = } to disambiguate same-named objects); the levelized
cost section applies to technology, storage and trade only.

}}
\examples{
\dontrun{
open_project(tempdir())

ek  <- topia$modules$electricity$R3
tech <- ek$ECOA

# an object on its own: its assumptions, and an ex-ante estimate of what it
# could do
report(tech)

# the same object as the model sees it -- prices and calendar from the
# model it belongs to
mod <- newModel("TOPIA", data = ek$repo,
                calendar = topia$modules$calendars$s4_h24,
                region = ek$regions, horizon = topia$modules$horizons$base)
mod <- setGeoscale(mod, ek$geoscale)
report(tech, model = mod)

# and as a solved scenario realized it, against that ex-ante estimate
scen <- solve_model(mod, name = "BASE", solver = solver_options$glpk)
report(tech, scenario = scen)

# with a map of where it is sited
report(tech, model = mod, geoscale = topia$geoscales$squares)

# a container reports what the container is about: a model its
# assumptions, a scenario its results
report(mod)
report(scen)

# other formats, and several at once
report(tech, format = "pdf")
report(tech, format = c("html", "docx"))
}
}
